# Strategy Engine Governance (Permanent)

**Status:** Permanent platform invariant · part of **Studio Governance FROZEN · Maintenance Mode**  
**Constitution:** `docs/architecture/STUDIO_CAPABILITY_CONTRACT.md`  
**Code:** `features/campaign-studio/strategy-engine/`  
**Type SSOT:** `PlanningContext` (`types/planning-context.ts`)  
**Product alias:** “Planning Session” = `PlanningContext` (same type; not a second entity)

Planning Context is an **internal runtime orchestration layer**.

## MUST NEVER

Planning Context must **never**:

- become a database table
- become a CRM business object
- become a Studio document
- become a saved entity
- own business state
- duplicate business artifacts (Campaign, Media Plan, Proposal, Presentation, Outputs, Budget, Brief, Objectives, etc.)

## MAY ONLY

Planning Context may **only**:

- orchestrate capabilities
- maintain runtime state
- coordinate planning entry points
- coordinate capability interactions
- project Planning Views (`derivePlanningView` — ephemeral, never persist)
- apply validated changes back to canonical Platform objects (Campaign Object, Media Plan via `lib/media-plan`, Outputs registry, optional CRM Campaign Header pointer)

## Persistence

All persistent business data remains owned by existing Platform objects.  
There is **no** Planning Context / Planning Session persistence vehicle.

## Violation

Violation of this rule requires **Architecture Reopen**.  
Do not “evolve” Planning Context into a document, table, or parallel SSOT without that reopen.
